{
  "_comment": "Dev-only fixture for site/inbox/. serve.py answers POST /api/inbox from this file when INBOX_FIXTURE names it, whatever the passphrase. Shapes follow api/inbox.js: list -> {inbox, cards}, numbers -> the nine views. Production never reads it.",
  "list": {
    "inbox": [
      {
        "blocker_id": 41,
        "n": 2,
        "card_id": 118,
        "title": "Wireless flashing for the second X4 Pro",
        "app": "developer-mode",
        "kind": "task",
        "state": "working",
        "body": "The first unit flashes over Wi-Fi from three trees. The second has never been paired, so every session that needs it still queues for the cable.\nsince: wifi-flash.sh --pair works on unit A; unit B untouched",
        "ask": "Pair the unit by the window. It needs its six-digit code read off the screen once; after that no session touches the cable.",
        "default": "The second unit stays on the cable and sessions that need it queue for the desk.",
        "steps": "1. On the device: Settings > System > Developer Mode > On\n2. Read the six digits it shows under the title\n3. Type them in the answer box and Send\n4. Leave it on the desk, off the cable; the session flashes it over Wi-Fi from here",
        "created_at": "2026-09-01T20:50:00Z"
      },
      {
        "blocker_id": 44,
        "n": 1,
        "card_id": 131,
        "title": "Wavelength ships the retail deck",
        "app": "wavelength",
        "kind": "feature",
        "state": "review",
        "body": "The prototype's prompt pairs were typed from the retail Wavelength deck during the design round, and nothing in the repository records permission to ship them. The game is otherwise done: two cold critics played it to the end, the board is public as agreed, and the four ideas the critic rounds killed stay dead.\nsince: 120 original pairs written on app/wavelength-deck and reviewed; three rewritten for being too close to retail wording",
        "ask": "Two decks exist and one has to ship in v1.13. The retail deck is the 96 pairs typed from the box, funnier, and not ours; shipping it means a credit line in About and a risk nobody here can size. The original deck is 120 pairs written on app/wavelength-deck, reviewed twice, three pairs rewritten for reading like the retail ones, and it is ours outright. Playtests split: the retail pairs got more laughs, the original pairs produced fewer stalls where the psychic could not place the clue at all. Which deck ships, or should both ship with retail behind a toggle that defaults off?",
        "default": "v1.13 ships the original deck; the retail pairs stay on a branch that never merges.",
        "steps": null,
        "created_at": "2026-09-02T19:20:00Z"
      },
      {
        "blocker_id": 47,
        "n": 1,
        "card_id": 140,
        "title": "Trivia category label on the shelf",
